{"data": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2122775622699393024"]}, "author_id": "2588345408", "created_at": "2026-11-17T19:35:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122775745042997380"], "id": "2122775745042997380", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 3338, "like_count": 17, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Bloomberg: A new US licensing rule has frozen a $480M loan to buy Nvidia GPUs that ByteDance would use in Malaysia.\n\nSingapore neocloud Aolani Cloud was arranging the 3-year loan through DBS Group.\n\nOn Monday, Washington began requiring data center operators in Singapore, https://t.co/6TJTdcpPbt", "url": "https://x.com/rohanpaul_ai/status/2122775745042997380"}, {"author_id": "2588345408", "created_at": "2026-11-17T19:32:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122774990311637213"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 108, "id": "2096990866028089344", "start": 97, "username": "VersineApp"}], "urls": [{"end": 303, "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/ZISz6EoVIx"}]}, "id": "2122774990311637213", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1514, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2122713860973150622", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "MCP is becoming the place where agents get real permissions, and money is the obvious next one.\n\n@VersineApp (YC F26)  connects a funded payment account to ChatGPT, Claude, Muse, Instinct or any MCP client, so the agent can send and request money as ordinary tool calls.\n\nHanding https://t.co/ZISz6EoVIx", "url": "https://x.com/rohanpaul_ai/status/2122774990311637213"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2122772780995493888"]}, "author_id": "2588345408", "created_at": "2026-11-17T19:25:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122773095010468026"], "id": "2122773095010468026", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 19, "impression_count": 2609, "like_count": 27, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "New Harvard paper finds that 94.8% of a coding agent's tokens were re-reads of cached context, i.e. 94.8% of the text the AI processed was earlier conversation it was re-reading, not new work.\n\nAnd that re-reading raises its estimated energy use about 25 times, from roughly 10 to https://t.co/C5LmE2RV8v", "url": "https://x.com/rohanpaul_ai/status/2122773095010468026"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2122772177720336384"]}, "author_id": "2588345408", "created_at": "2026-11-17T19:23:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122772518683779524"], "id": "2122772518683779524", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 1950, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "New Amazon +  University of Massachusetts  paper finds that adding an LLM critic to a search loop has small upside, about 0.005 AUC at best, and much larger downside.\n\nWeak LLM critic can push AutoML search below plain random search\n\nAgent systems often add an LLM critic that https://t.co/IYNxbw4Y7D", "url": "https://x.com/rohanpaul_ai/status/2122772518683779524"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2122768866971709441", "3_2122768905836126208"]}, "author_id": "2588345408", "created_at": "2026-11-17T19:14:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122770273879658621"], "entities": {"urls": [{"end": 327, "start": 304, "url": "https://t.co/c89pLcLz8Y"}]}, "id": "2122770273879658621", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 2047, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2122318031162647001", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "A new open source decision model just launched, and it ranks first out of 300.\n\nKarpo-Decision-31B swaps decoding for a readout head: a single-token code per option, one score per code, a softmax over that question's options. Zero generated tokens, always a valid answer, and the https://t.co/TNvDwJuaxZ https://t.co/c89pLcLz8Y", "url": "https://x.com/rohanpaul_ai/status/2122770273879658621"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2122763260818841600"]}, "author_id": "1743487864934162432", "created_at": "2026-11-17T18:48:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122763792828555299"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 91, "id": "74286565", "start": 81, "username": "Microsoft"}]}, "id": "2122763792828555299", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 25, "impression_count": 21796, "like_count": 167, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 10}, "text": "Microsoft-Decision-1.1 scores 68 on the Artificial Analysis Decision Index v2.1\n\n@Microsoft has released Microsoft-Decision-1.1, an update to their existing decision model, Microsoft-Decision-1. It remains priced at $0.042 per one million input tokens.\n\nKey results:\n\n➤ https://t.co/B8qrosvfmK", "url": "https://x.com/ArtificialAnlys/status/2122763792828555299"}, {"author_id": "1825243643529027584", "created_at": "2026-11-17T18:46:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122762987589021866", "2122763237124899201"], "entities": {"urls": [{"end": 106, "start": 83, "url": "https://t.co/d0aPwJDfkn"}]}, "id": "2122763237124899201", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 46, "impression_count": 17850, "like_count": 211, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 8}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2122762411287748696", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "loopy loopy\n\nI told you loopmaxxers are the next paradigm. It's only up from here. https://t.co/d0aPwJDfkn", "url": "https://x.com/scaling01/status/2122763237124899201"}, {"author_id": "1825243643529027584", "created_at": "2026-11-17T18:45:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122762987589021866", "2122763237124899201"], "entities": {"urls": [{"end": 69, "start": 46, "url": "https://t.co/d0aPwJDfkn"}]}, "id": "2122762987589021866", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 695, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2122762411287748696", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "loopy loopy\n\nI told you we are on a new trend https://t.co/d0aPwJDfkn", "url": "https://x.com/scaling01/status/2122762987589021866"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2122762184283545600"]}, "author_id": "2588345408", "created_at": "2026-11-17T18:43:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122762448260501600"], "entities": {"urls": [{"end": 325, "start": 302, "url": "https://t.co/PmTZU3Mgu2"}]}, "id": "2122762448260501600", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 3011, "like_count": 15, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2122496000510320659", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Dario Amodei spends 40% to 50% of his time on talent and culture.\n\nIncluding a talk to the whole company every 2 weeks called DVQ (Dario Vision Quest) where he speaks with no corporate speak, and a culture interview that turns away brilliant engineers who are jerks.\n\n----\nFull https://t.co/qpnLkb38OW https://t.co/PmTZU3Mgu2", "url": "https://x.com/rohanpaul_ai/status/2122762448260501600"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2122760473359560704", "3_2122760636786454528"]}, "author_id": "1825243643529027584", "created_at": "2026-11-17T18:37:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2122761003385729331"], "entities": {"urls": [{"end": 302, "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/Uuv6eKo0JT"}]}, "id": "2122761003385729331", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 5367, "like_count": 83, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2122753742781198554", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Astra 6.2 is now even better at solving problems without visible reasoning\n\nroughly 2x better odds of solving a given problem compared to Astra 6\n\nand \"EpochAI found thatGPT-6.2 Astra was able to perform 12.3 serial steps, compared to GPT-6 Astra's 10.5\" https://t.co/nv65gDjlu5 https://t.co/Uuv6eKo0JT", "url": "https://x.com/scaling01/